commit c40ba5f8a9b0eac9311f3c7c81ce64e440b66b45

C03: display.status reads the attached monitors (resolution, count, refresh rate) (SYSTEM1459)

SYSTEM1301 documented that «qué resolución tengo» (H0195), «qué resolución de pantalla tengo» (H0464), «cuántos monitores tengo» (H0707) and «Que Hz tiene el monitor?» (H0125) had no display scope in system.status: new infrastructure was needed.

Baxy.Kernel ProductCatalog: descriptor display.status (no arguments, ReadOnly, verifier display.status.windows.display.devices.read.v1), in ordinal order between clipboard.write.text and email.latest.read.
Baxy.Core ExternalCapabilityHandlers: the operation is handled.
Baxy.Providers.Windows WindowsDeviceControlAdapter: DisplayStatus enumerates the display devices attached to the desktop through the Win32 display API (EnumDisplayDevicesW, EnumDisplaySettingsW with the current mode) and reports seen.monitorCount and seen.monitors[] with name, primary, width, height and refreshHz — a read, nothing changed; WindowsExternalCapabilityProvider maps its unavailability reason.
baxy_mind effect_intent: _display_status_question reads the resolution question («qué resolución (de pantalla) tengo», «cuál es la resolución de mi pantalla»), the count question («cuántos monitores/pantallas tengo/hay») and the refresh-rate question («qué Hz tiene el monitor», «a cuántos Hz va la pantalla», «qué frecuencia de refresco tiene el monitor») as a display.status read — never a change (brightness or set/change words excluded), accepted as a direct request and grounded by the display nouns.
baxy_mind __main__: the read takes no arguments.
baxy_mind llm: an instruction names seen.monitors and seen.monitorCount and asks for only the requested number; the reply may carry no number that is not observed (invented_number, with a hint) and must carry the asked one — width and height for a resolution question, refreshHz for a Hz question, the count (digit or word) for a how-many question (missing_state).
Catalog aliases: one row (alias_count 160); documentación/base/05_MATRIZ_EJECUCION.json: the read is registered as read-only without effect.

Offline probes: a ctypes probe of the same Win32 structures reports this laptop's single 1920x1080 display at 144 Hz with the struct sizes 840 and 220 the adapter assumes; the four literals and six variants resolve to one display.status; the boundaries resolve to nothing and «No cambies la resolución.» is a prohibition; over that observation, «Tienes una resolución de 2560 x 1440» and «El monitor tiene 60 Hz» are vetoed as invented numbers, «Tienes dos monitores» misses the state, and the faithful replies pass. Providers project compiled clean before sealing (build servers shut down). Kernel, Core, Providers and App recompiled (BUILD1459). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


